{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Please let her not be like a dead one.</b> Like a metzora who was afflicted with tzara'at upon emerging from his mother's womb, who has no purification ever; but this one, who was afflicted only on account of the sin of lashon hara, it is effective for her [i.e., she can be healed], as we find with Pharaoh, who was afflicted with tzara'at on account of Sarah and was healed when he restored her."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:20.486189910Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}